Well, now that you mention it, Medusa shouldn't be bothered by her
reflection.  First of all, Perseus could look at her reflection in his
polished shield (that's how he aimed his killing stroke) and not be
bothered; Medusa's reflection was not enough to kill.  Second, in the
myth, Medusa shared her island with two Gorgon half-sisters, who
looked much like her (and had the same petrifying effect).  She wasn't
killed by looking at *them*.  How about it, dev team?

BTW:  In the myth, Medusa's severed head was still petrifying.
(Athena mounted it on her shield; any mortal who looked on it was
turned to stone.)  In the game, does her corpse have this effect?  (I
don't know because I always kill her while blindfolded, and don't take
off the blindfold until I've tinned the corpse/pickaxed the
statue/etc.  My thirst for abstract knowledge is not strong enought
for me to try the experiment.

Also, one of Medusa's attacks ought to be poisonous (the asps on her
head).  Not that anyone would make it that far without poison
resistance...


